Z||000000||MotherGoose||04-11-2001||01:19 PM||||Is it possible to put a vette engine with a 6-speed in these wonderful little cars?<P>I am thinking of doing this because the vette can get upwards of 30mpg at 70 miles per hour.<P>thanks<P>The Goose||||reg||1
Z||000001||EdsB52||04-11-2001||02:20 PM||||Tell me about it! I just bought a 94 Z-28 w/an LT-1 and a 6 speed. At 100 mph, it tachs at 2400 rpm in 6th gear. I'm no swap expert, but I think you would have to put the engine in the front of the car and an axle in the rear, which I've yet to see. I have seen engines installed in-line w/a transaxle that turns the output 90 degrees. They stretch the car a foot or two by splicing into the frame. They sell adapter plates to put different engines in front of trannys, but I don't know how you would easily use that 6speed trans in a transverse application. I'm sure you'll agree, that tranny makes the car. I love my 6speed. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||04-11-2001||02:29 PM||||Celica 6spd GTS FWD tranny is one I have been looking into and have a bit of info on.<P>As well there are a few kits out there for VW VR6 trannies to be converted to 6spd , plus they sell kits to make them handle upwards of 400ft lbs TQ<P>the T56 is a nice tranny , but a fwd 6spd unit would be less of an engineering project<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||04-11-2001||02:32 PM||||What do you know about the Celica 6 speed?<BR>I would have thought two things:<BR>a) It's put behind a gutless 4 cylinder and is geared way too short for a torquey engine. IOW, no advantage over a Getrag.<P>b) It's not strong enough for a V8, although it could probably handle a V6.<P>I could be wrong.<BR>What have you heard?||||reg||1
